TEST_LIVE_PLANS=1 env var gates against actual plan files\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 straightforward fixture replacement.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] No absolute `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2` paths remain in any test file\\n- [ ] Tests use either `tmp_path`-based synthetic fixtures OR a `SAM_TEST_LIVE_PLANS=1` env-var gate for live file access\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_readers/ -x` runs (not skips) all three test files in CI\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_readers/` \u2014 zero errors\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_readers/test_detect.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_readers/test_frontmatter_reader.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_readers/test_manifest_reader.py`\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a **CI pipeline running the SAM reader tests**, I want **machine-specific absolute paths replaced with portable fixtures** so that **skipped tests become executable tests that actually catch regressions**.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix machine-specific hardcoded paths in sam reader tests** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Test quality audit 2026-03-29\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"edd451a0b8f7eed02ba7329138d3c0ab5b11b46183b691af5e2a8ac8f7773cc0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS8cRA\"}"}